Subject: [PATCH 06967/11362] Task 9 follow-on: wire
 InertClickSigPruner.rank_candidates + observe into
 StepwiseExplorer/E3AgentPolicy (REQ-ARC-FCP-5595)

Closes the loose end task 9's own DONE note flagged: rank_candidates matched
StepwiseExplorer._candidates's filter-protocol shape but was never actually
wired in. Added coerce_inert_click_pruner (matching
coerce_program_synthesis_filter's None/False/instance/True-constructs-default
shape), threaded inert_click_pruner through both StepwiseExplorer and
E3AgentPolicy, and added a rank_candidates call in _candidates alongside
program_synthesis_filter/goal_candidate_guidance.

Also wired a real observe() call into _ingest's existing per-transition
OBSERVE hook (the same site feeding dense_curiosity/controllable_novelty_
policy/object_centric_proposal_policy/action_prior) -- without this the
filter would be wired but permanently a no-op, since the pruner's tally never
accumulates evidence from live play.

Gated OFF by default (SUBMITTED_INERT_CLICK_PRUNER_ENABLED = False, mirrored
in SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG), matching every other freshly-wired-but-
unvalidated component in arc_competition_agent.py -- flipping it on for the
scored agent needs its own matched-budget offline A/B first, per the
solve_rate_dropped guardrail.

8 new tests (test_arc_inert_click_pruner_live_wiring.py); 46+ pre-existing
arc_competition_agent.py-adjacent tests (submitted-parity, program-synthesis
filter, E3 fidelity/named-tail gates, HUD mask, competition-agent adapter)
still pass unchanged. Spec additions: REQ-ARC-FCP-5595's spec.md section
gets a WIRING FOLLOW-ON note plus three new SCENARIOs.

(The core code changes -- arc_inert_click_pruner.py, arc_competition_agent.py,
and this test file's initial version -- were already captured by the
conductor's own concurrent commits via its git-add-everything behavior; this
commit adds the remaining coverage-completing test case plus the spec docs.
ops/known-issues.md's task-9 addendum is NOT included here -- blocked again
by the same overdue-priority-lint as the earlier task-8 commit; left staged
on disk.)

